A host hands each provider the stored model catalogue the store already
copied, without cloning it a second time.

Each conversation's start refreshes its providers' models twice, once
from the store alone and once over the network, and each time the store
returns a copy of the provider's catalogue that pi-ai then clones again.
With a few providers signed in the catalogues come to about 336 KB of
JSON, and the second clone alone costs about 0.07 s of every wake. Every store pi ships already answers
with a copy of its own, so the provider can't change what the store
holds either way.

Apply only to the host's private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays
unchanged.

--- a/packages/ai/src/models.ts
+++ b/packages/ai/src/models.ts
@@ -553,7 +553,9 @@ class ModelsImpl implements MutableModels {
 		const stored = await this.modelsStore.read(provider.id, { signal });
 		await provider.refreshModels({
 			credential,
-			stored: stored ? withKnownModelTypes(structuredClone(stored)) : undefined,
+			// pi-host: every models store pi ships hands back a copy of its own, so cloning it again
+			// here only doubled what each conversation's start spent copying its providers' catalogues.
+			stored: stored ? withKnownModelTypes(stored) : undefined,
 			publish: (publication) => this.publishProviderModels(provider.id, generation, signal, publication),
 			allowNetwork,
 			force: allowNetwork ? force : undefined,
